  "notes": [
    "T is the day of transaction and refers to the calendar date (circular, general instruction 4). TAT is the outer limit; banks 'shall endeavour towards quicker resolution'.",
    "RBI's table does not use the words P2P or P2M. Row 4a is 'transfer of funds'; row 4b is 'payment to merchant'. This card replaces the demo card RBI-TAT-UPI-P2P and corrects who reverses: the BENEFICIARY bank, not the originating bank.",
    "effective_from is the circular's issue date; the operative date inside the circular was not recorded.",
    "The RBI circular of 4 Jun 2020 (DPSS 1897) temporarily read 'calendar days' as 'working days' only until 31 Dec 2020, so it has lapsed (regulations/rbi-payments/RBI_2020-06-04_extension-timeline-payment-systems-dpss1897.html).",
    "The 2019 circular cites the 'Integrated Ombudsman Scheme, 2021 (as amended)'. A 2026 scheme is reported to have replaced it; see RBI-OMB-ESCALATION.",
    "Tier A matchers live in check.config.matchers (added by the engine build): regex lists per language, phrase lists and negation cues. All Hinglish/Hindi variants and typo patterns are engineering-authored and UNREVIEWED: a native-speaker compliance reviewer must approve them before activation."
  ],
  "open_issues": [
